IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-3-punishments`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 8 -- Offences relating to unlawful assembly`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 141, 142, 143, 144, 145, 146, 147, 148, 149, 150, 151, 152, 153,
-- 154, 155, 156, 157, 158.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- The Chapter is built on two definitions and one deeming rule. s 141 says what an
-- UNLAWFUL ASSEMBLY is: 5 or more persons with one of five common objects. s 142 says
-- who is a MEMBER of it: one who, aware of the facts that make it unlawful,
-- intentionally joins or continues in it. s 146 makes every member guilty of RIOTING
-- when force or violence is used by the assembly or any member in prosecution of the
-- common object. Everything else attaches to those: punishment for membership
-- (s 143) and for rioting (s 147); the armed aggravations (ss 144, 148); continuing
-- after a command to disperse (s 145, and s 151 for an assembly that is merely likely
-- to disturb the peace); constructive liability for an offence committed in
-- prosecution of the common object (s 149); hiring members (s 150), harbouring hired
-- persons (s 157) and being hired (s 158); obstructing a public servant dispersing
-- one (s 152); provoking a riot (s 153); and the duties of the landowner, the
-- beneficiary and their agents (ss 154 to 156).
--
-- s 141's Explanation -- an assembly not unlawful when it assembled may become one --
-- adds no limb: the test is on the common object, whenever it was formed.
--
-- s 151's Explanation says that where the assembly is an unlawful assembly within
-- s 141 the offender is punishable under s 145. That routes punishment; it does not
-- narrow s 151's own words, so s 151 is encoded on its own facts and a s 145 case can
-- satisfy both. Neither section's punishment is computed, so the routing has nothing
-- to act on here.
--
-- ss 143 and 147 are punishment sections and are computed here with the Chapter 3
-- vocabulary. The internal punishment splits of ss 153 and 158 are carried as facts
-- and not decided.

§§ `Section 141 -- Unlawful assembly`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 141"
@export Decide whether the assembly is an unlawful assembly under Penal Code 1871 section 141
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc An assembly of 5 or more persons whose common object is one of the five in s 141(a) to (e): overawing the Government or a public servant by criminal force, resisting the execution of law or legal process, committing an offence, taking property or depriving of a right by criminal force, or compelling a person by criminal force to do what he is not bound to or omit what he is entitled to.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assembly is an unlawful assembly` IF
        ua's `the assembly is of 5 or more persons`
    AND (   ua's `the common object is to overawe by criminal force or show of criminal force the Legislative or Executive Government or any public servant in the exercise of his lawful power`
         OR ua's `the common object is to resist the execution of any law or of any legal process`
         OR ua's `the common object is to commit any offence`
         OR ua's `the common object is by criminal force or show of criminal force to any person to take or obtain possession of property or to deprive any person of the enjoyment of a right of way or of the use of water or other incorporeal right in his possession or enjoyment or to enforce any right or supposed right`
         OR ua's `the common object is by criminal force or show of criminal force to compel any person to do what he is not legally bound to do or to omit to do what he is legally entitled to do`)

§§ `Sections 142 and 143 -- Membership, and its punishment`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 142"
@export Decide whether the person is a member of an unlawful assembly under Penal Code 1871 section 142
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc Being aware of facts which render the assembly unlawful, and intentionally joining it or continuing in it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a member of an unlawful assembly` IF
        `the assembly is an unlawful assembly` ua
    AND ua's `is aware of facts which render the assembly an unlawful assembly`
    AND ua's `intentionally joins the assembly or continues in it`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 143"
@export Give the punishment for being a member of an unlawful assembly under Penal Code 1871 section 143
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for membership of an unlawful assembly` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine or both` 2

§§ `Sections 144 and 145 -- Armed members, and continuing after a command to disperse`

-- The s 144 Illustration -- a wooden pole sharpened at the end is a thing likely to
-- cause death when used as a weapon -- is applied to ss 148 and 158 as well, and the
-- armed fact is shared by all three.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 144"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes joining an unlawful assembly armed with a deadly weapon under Penal Code 1871 section 144
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc A member of an unlawful assembly who is armed with a deadly weapon or with anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes membership of an unlawful assembly while armed` IF
        `the person is a member of an unlawful assembly` ua
    AND ua's `is armed with a deadly weapon or with anything which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 145"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes joining or continuing in an unlawful assembly knowing it has been commanded to disperse under Penal Code 1871 section 145
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc Joining or continuing in an unlawful assembly, knowing that it has been commanded in the manner prescribed by law to disperse.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes continuing in an unlawful assembly after a command to disperse` IF
        `the assembly is an unlawful assembly` ua
    AND ua's `joins or continues in the assembly`
    AND ua's `knows that the unlawful assembly has been commanded in the manner prescribed by law to disperse`

§§ `Sections 146 to 148 -- Rioting`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 146"
@export Decide whether the person is guilty of rioting under Penal Code 1871 section 146
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc Every member of an unlawful assembly is guilty of rioting whenever force or violence is used by the assembly or any member of it in prosecution of the common object.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of rioting` IF
        `the person is a member of an unlawful assembly` ua
    AND ua's `force or violence is used by the assembly or by any member of it in prosecution of the common object`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 147"
@export Give the punishment for rioting under Penal Code 1871 section 147
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for rioting` MEANS `imprisonment up to and liable to caning` 7

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 148"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes rioting armed with a deadly weapon under Penal Code 1871 section 148
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc Rioting while armed with a deadly weapon or with anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes rioting while armed` IF
        `the person is guilty of rioting` ua
    AND ua's `is armed with a deadly weapon or with anything which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death`

§§ `Section 149 -- Every member guilty of an offence committed in prosecution of the common object`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 149"
@export Decide whether Penal Code 1871 section 149 makes the member guilty of an offence committed by another member in prosecution of the common object
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc An offence committed by a member of the unlawful assembly in prosecution of the common object, or one the members knew to be likely to be committed in prosecution of it, and the person being a s 142 member of the same assembly at the time.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is guilty under section 149 of the offence committed in prosecution of the common object` IF
        `the person is a member of an unlawful assembly` ua
    AND ua's `an offence is committed by a member of the assembly in prosecution of the common object or such as the members knew to be likely to be committed in prosecution of that object`
    AND ua's `is a member of the same assembly at the time that offence is committed`

§§ `Section 150 -- Hiring persons to join an unlawful assembly`

-- The hirer is punishable as a member of the assembly, and for any offence
-- committed by the hired person as a member in pursuance of the hiring, as if he had
-- been a member or committed the offence himself. The liability is decided; the
-- "punishable as" is punishment.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 150"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes hiring or conniving at the hiring of persons to join an unlawful assembly under Penal Code 1871 section 150
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc Hiring, engaging, employing, or promoting or conniving at the hiring, engagement or employment of any person to join or become a member of an unlawful assembly.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes hiring persons to join an unlawful assembly` IF
        `the assembly is an unlawful assembly` ua
    AND ua's `hires engages employs or promotes or connives at the hiring engagement or employment of any person to join or become a member of the unlawful assembly`

§§ `Section 151 -- Continuing in an assembly of 5 or more likely to disturb the peace after a command to disperse`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 151"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes knowingly joining or continuing in an assembly of 5 or more persons after it has been commanded to disperse under Penal Code 1871 section 151
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc An assembly of 5 or more persons likely to cause a disturbance of the public peace, lawfully commanded to disperse, which the person knowingly joins or continues in after the command. Needs no s 141 common object.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes continuing in an assembly likely to disturb the peace after a command to disperse` IF
        ua's `the assembly is of 5 or more persons likely to cause a disturbance of the public peace`
    AND ua's `the assembly has been lawfully commanded to disperse and the person knowingly joins or continues in it after the command`

§§ `Sections 152 and 153 -- Obstructing suppression, and provoking a riot`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 152"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes assaulting or obstructing a public servant suppressing a riot or dispersing an unlawful assembly under Penal Code 1871 section 152
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc Assaulting, threatening to assault, obstructing or attempting to obstruct a public servant discharging his duty to disperse an unlawful assembly or suppress a riot or affray, or using or threatening or attempting criminal force to him.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes obstructing a public servant suppressing a riot` IF
    ua's `assaults or threatens to assault or obstructs or attempts to obstruct a public servant in the discharge of his duty in endeavouring to disperse an unlawful assembly or to suppress a riot or an affray or uses or threatens or attempts to use criminal force to such public servant`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 153"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes intentionally or rashly giving provocation with intent to cause a riot under Penal Code 1871 section 153
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc Intentionally or rashly, by doing anything illegal, giving provocation to any person, intending or knowing it likely that the provocation will cause rioting. Whether rioting follows affects punishment only.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes provocation with intent to cause a riot` IF
        ua's `intentionally or rashly by doing anything which is illegal gives provocation to any person`
    AND ua's `intends or knows it to be likely that the provocation will cause the offence of rioting to be committed`

§§ `Sections 154 to 156 -- The owner or occupier, the beneficiary, and their agents`

-- s 154 is read as it is written. The owner, occupier or claimant is punishable if
-- he or his agent, knowing of or having reason to expect the assembly or riot, does
-- not give the earliest notice to the police, AND does not (having reason to believe
-- it about to be committed) use all lawful means to prevent it, AND does not (in the
-- event of its taking place) use all lawful means to disperse or suppress it. The
-- three omissions are conjoined because the section conjoins them; a reading that
-- makes any one omission enough is the alternative NOTES.md records.
--
-- ss 155 and 156 are the same duty on a different person: the one for whose benefit
-- or on whose behalf the riot is committed (s 155), and that person's agent or
-- manager (s 156). Each is punishable if, having reason to believe the riot or the
-- assembly likely, he does not use all lawful means to prevent it and to suppress and
-- disperse it.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 154"
@export Decide whether the owner or occupier of land on which an unlawful assembly is held or a riot committed is liable under Penal Code 1871 section 154
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc An unlawful assembly or riot on land; the person being its owner, occupier or a claimant of an interest; knowledge or reason to expect the offence; and the failure of him or his agent to give the earliest notice to the police, to use all lawful means to prevent it, and to use all lawful means to disperse or suppress it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes an owner or occupier failing to notify prevent or suppress an unlawful assembly or riot` IF
        ua's `an unlawful assembly is held or a riot is committed on land`
    AND ua's `is the owner or occupier of the land or has or claims an interest in it`
    AND ua's `he or his agent or manager knows that the offence is being or has been committed or has reason to believe it is likely to be committed`
    AND NOT ua's `he or his agent or manager gives the earliest notice in his power to the principal officer at the nearest police station`
    AND NOT ua's `he or his agent or manager having reason to believe the offence is about to be committed uses all lawful means in his power to prevent it`
    AND NOT ua's `he or his agent or manager in the event of the offence taking place uses all lawful means in his power to disperse or suppress it`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 155"
@export Decide whether the person for whose benefit a riot is committed is liable under Penal Code 1871 section 155
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc A riot committed for the benefit or on behalf of the owner, occupier, claimant or beneficiary; the person being that person; and the failure of him or his agent, having reason to believe the riot or assembly likely, to use all lawful means to prevent, suppress and disperse it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a beneficiary of a riot failing to prevent or suppress it` IF
        ua's `a riot is committed for the benefit or on behalf of a person who is the owner or occupier of land respecting which the riot takes place or who claims an interest in the land or in the subject of the dispute which gave rise to the riot or who has accepted or derived any benefit from it`
    AND ua's `is that person`
    AND ua's `he or his agent or manager has reason to believe that the riot was likely to be committed or that the unlawful assembly by which it was committed was likely to be held`
    AND NOT ua's `he or his agent or manager uses all lawful means in his power to prevent the riot or assembly from taking place and to suppress and disperse it`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 156"
@export Decide whether the agent or manager of the person for whose benefit a riot is committed is liable under Penal Code 1871 section 156
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc The same riot, the person being the agent or manager of the beneficiary, and the agent or manager's own failure, having reason to believe the riot or assembly likely, to use all lawful means to prevent, suppress and disperse it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes an agent of a beneficiary of a riot failing to prevent or suppress it` IF
        ua's `a riot is committed for the benefit or on behalf of a person who is the owner or occupier of land respecting which the riot takes place or who claims an interest in the land or in the subject of the dispute which gave rise to the riot or who has accepted or derived any benefit from it`
    AND ua's `is the agent or manager of that person`
    AND ua's `he or his agent or manager has reason to believe that the riot was likely to be committed or that the unlawful assembly by which it was committed was likely to be held`
    AND NOT ua's `he or his agent or manager uses all lawful means in his power to prevent the riot or assembly from taking place and to suppress and disperse it`

§§ `Sections 157 and 158 -- Harbouring hired persons, and being hired`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 157"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes harbouring persons hired for an unlawful assembly under Penal Code 1871 section 157
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc Harbouring, receiving or assembling in premises under his occupation, charge or control persons known to have been or to be about to be hired to join an unlawful assembly, intending to permit or facilitate their joining or to screen them from punishment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes harbouring persons hired for an unlawful assembly` IF
        ua's `harbours receives or assembles in a house or premises in his occupation or charge or under his control persons knowing that they have been or are about to be hired engaged or employed to join or become members of an unlawful assembly`
    AND ua's `intends to permit or facilitate them joining or becoming members of an unlawful assembly or to screen them or any of them from punishment`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 158"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes being hired to take part in an unlawful assembly or riot under Penal Code 1871 section 158
GIVEN ua IS AN `Unlawful Assembly` @desc Being engaged or hired, or offering or attempting to be, to do or assist in any of the s 141 acts. Going armed is the aggravated limb and affects punishment only.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes being hired for an unlawful assembly` IF
    ua's `is engaged or hired or offers or attempts to be hired or engaged to do or assist in doing any of the acts specified in section 141`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes membership of an unlawful assembly` IF
        (   `the person is a member of an unlawful assembly` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `constitutes membership of an unlawful assembly while armed` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `constitutes continuing in an unlawful assembly after a command to disperse` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `constitutes continuing in an assembly likely to disturb the peace after a command to disperse` (a's `unlawful assembly`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes rioting` IF
        (   `the person is guilty of rioting` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `constitutes rioting while armed` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `the member is guilty under section 149 of the offence committed in prosecution of the common object` (a's `unlawful assembly`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes an offence ancillary to an unlawful assembly or riot` IF
        (   `constitutes hiring persons to join an unlawful assembly` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `constitutes obstructing a public servant suppressing a riot` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `constitutes provocation with intent to cause a riot` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `constitutes an owner or occupier failing to notify prevent or suppress an unlawful assembly or riot` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `constitutes a beneficiary of a riot failing to prevent or suppress it` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `constitutes an agent of a beneficiary of a riot failing to prevent or suppress it` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `constitutes harbouring persons hired for an unlawful assembly` (a's `unlawful assembly`)
         OR `constitutes being hired for an unlawful assembly` (a's `unlawful assembly`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
